Description: Skip the keyboard enhancement probe, which hangs startup inside tmux
 0.8.0 asks the terminal whether it speaks the Kitty keyboard protocol before
 drawing its first frame. Inside tmux (3.5a, 3.7c and 3.8 measured) the process
 then stays blocked in a read on the terminal and never draws; 0.7.0, which has
 no probe, starts normally. Skipping the probe makes 0.8.0 draw again.
 .
 What it costs is the protocol itself, which upstream's comment says lets keys
 like Ctrl+Tab and Ctrl+I arrive as themselves rather than as the plainer key a
 legacy terminal sends. Drop this patch once upstream fixes the hang.
Author: pkg.haus archive <archive@pkg.haus>
Bug: https://github.com/iamrohithrnair/emeraldian/issues/47
Forwarded: https://github.com/iamrohithrnair/emeraldian/issues/47
Last-Update: 2026-10-23
--- a/crates/emeraldian/src/main.rs
+++ b/crates/emeraldian/src/main.rs
@@ -399,10 +399,7 @@
     // `Ctrl+Tab` or `Ctrl+I` instead of the plainer key a legacy terminal
     // sends in their place. Asked for only where it is understood, so other
     // terminals see nothing new.
-    let enhanced = matches!(
-        crossterm::terminal::supports_keyboard_enhancement(),
-        Ok(true)
-    );
+    let enhanced = false;
